  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: ResCoordDisc 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "You have been working with a research team that is reviewing patient
    samples from past studies that can be used to explore new ideas for cancer treatments,
    tracking consent and ensuring the team follows ethical and privacy standards.
    It is early in the research, but research coordinators are responsible for making
    sure any patient samples \u2014 like blood or tissue \u2014 are handled properly
    and used only for approved purposes.\n\nIs this true or false?"
  explanation: Even in the earliest stages, research coordinators are responsible
    for making sure that all patient samples are collected, stored, and used in an
    ethical and secure way. This means confirming that every sample was donated with
    informed consent, removing personal details to protect patient privacy, and ensuring
    samples are used only for approved studies. Their careful oversight helps keep
    research safe, responsible, and focused on advancing treatments that truly benefit
    patients and families.
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Research Coordinator
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Discovery
